{"n": 149, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "149.webp", "text": "11-261\n\n1165015 CHECKING BEARING PLAY\nOF TURBOCHARGER\n\nExcessive bearing play could be the\ncause for excessive oll In the turbo-\ncharger (which will be noticed on blue\nsmoke) or nolse.\n\nAxial play: max. 0.15 mm (0.006\").\nApply dial gage on turbocharger shaft\nand move shaft from stop to slop\nwithout turning.\n\nRadial play: max. 0.8 mm (0.031\").\nApply dial gage on turbocharger shaft.\nMove turbocharger shalt from stop to\nstop on both ends simultaneously\nwhile turning.\n\n1165018 CHECKING CHARGING\nPRESSURE OF TURBO-\nCHARGER\n\nmamometer Stand:\nCheck with help of DDE self-diagnosis\n(call status lists).\n\nOperate car in load range.\n\nTake charging pressure (absolute valoc\nIncluding atmospheric pressure) fram\nthe charging pressure sensor display.\nSpecification: max. 1650 + 50 mbar.\n\nChecking In Test Drive:\n\nConnect pressure tester, Special Tool\n13 5 000, between the intake manifdld\nand charging pressure sensor, and\nplace In the passenger compartment.\nMake sure thal the hose Is not pinched\nCheck charging pressure by driving\ncar In load range (braking).\nSpecification:\n\nMeasured charging pressure + atmos-\npheric pressure (see 1165...) = max\n1850 + 50 mbar.\n\nPossible Faults When Charging\n:\n\nPressure Is Not Correct;\n\nBypass regulator (see 11 65 059).\nCharging pressure sensor (see 11 65 ...)\nPressure converter (see 11 65. . .).\nHose connections (check for leaks with\n@ Spray).\n\nTurbocharger (shaft turns too hard,\nbypass).", "words": [["11-261", 0.4712, 0.0284, 0.544, 0.0549], ["1165015", 0.2705, 0.0694, 0.321, 0.0813], ["CHECKING", 0.3291, 0.0694, 0.3878, 0.0813], ["BEARING", 0.3928, 0.0694, 0.4439, 0.08], ["PLAY", 0.4479, 0.0694, 0.4772, 0.08], ["OF", 0.3291, 0.0853, 0.3443, 0.0979], ["TURBOCHARGER", 0.3483, 0.0853, 0.4439, 0.0979], ["Excessive", 0.2705, 0.1204, 0.3251, 0.1323], ["bearing", 0.3281, 0.1204, 0.3686, 0.1349], ["play", 0.3726, 0.1204, 0.3948, 0.1336]